      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why fpstore after routine call ? \n\u003d\u003d\u003e we don\u0027t allow FPU math operation in interrupt context and it should be in tasks.  \n\nFPU context will not saved if current_task (currently interrupted task) will resume after this interrupt.(we don\u0027t have to save it.) \nIf different task is scheduled, FPU context will be stored current_task\u0027s stack and new task\u0027s previously stored-FPU context(as well as CPU context) will be restored. \nCPU context should be stored(pusha) regardless.",
